            <div xml:id="d710">

                <pb facs="0667" n="655" xml:id="pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/12–2344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of
                            State to the Director of the Office of Near Eastern and African
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-23">December 23, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Murray</hi>: I had the memorandum you prepared
                    on Palestine with me when I saw the President yesterday. When I mentioned the
                    subject, he complimented us on the fine manner in which this problem had been
                    handled in his absence and then expressed the hope that he would not have to get
                    into it again for some time. It therefore seemed inappropriate for me to bring
                    up your memorandum and I think we should not send it over for the time being. It
                    can be worked into our general preparation for what is ahead which we shall be
                    undertaking on a broad scale in the Department in the next few weeks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d710-a1.xml" xpointer="d710-a1"/>
